From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 08:13:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Phase=206.1:=20AX301=20LED=20polarity=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20driver=20+=20comments?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AX301 LEDs are active-HIGH (pin HIGH = LED visible ON), opposite of
the in-code assumption.  Empirically verified during Phase 6 bring-up
on 2026-05-17 via the led_walker bring-up bitstream: with
`LED <= not "0001"`, the user observed "LED[0] dark, LED[1..3] lit"
which only resolves coherently under active-HIGH polarity.

Fix: drop the inversion (`LED <= dbg_leds` not `LED <= not dbg_leds`)
so LED visible ON corresponds to the debug-flag being set, matching
the intent stated in the comments.  Comments updated to active-HIGH
on the entity-port declaration and the debug-driver block.

No functional change beyond the LED visual: existing modes still
work, debug LEDs just now read in their natural sense rather than
needing mental inversion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 rtl/ax301_top.vhd | 17 ++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rtl/ax301_top.vhd b/rtl/ax301_top.vhd
index fb821ec..a253b05 100644
--- a/rtl/ax301_top.vhd
+++ b/rtl/ax301_top.vhd
@@ -27,7 +27,9 @@ entity ax301_top is
     -- UART (PL2303 → /dev/ttyUSB0)
     RXD    : in    std_ulogic;
     TXD    : out   std_ulogic;
-    -- LEDs (active-low, gpio_o[3:0])
+    -- LEDs (active-HIGH on AX301 — pin HIGH = LED visible ON;
+    -- see reference-ax301-board-quirks memory).  Empirically verified
+    -- with led_walker bring-up bitstream on 2026-05-17.
     LED    : out   std_ulogic_vector(3 downto 0);
     -- SDRAM (HY57V2562GTR, 32 MB)
     S_CLK  : out   std_ulogic;
@@ -275,16 +277,17 @@ begin
     spi_csn_o(7) => open
   );
 
-  -- DEBUG MODE: LEDs driven by XBUS debug latches (active-low on board)
-  -- LED ON = debug bit HIGH, LED OFF = debug bit LOW
+  -- DEBUG MODE: LEDs driven by XBUS debug latches (AX301 LEDs are
+  -- active-HIGH; pin HIGH = LED visible ON).  Drive pin directly from
+  -- the sticky/live flag so LED ON corresponds to "flag set".
   -- LED0: any XBUS request seen (sticky)
   -- LED1: SDRAM-addressed request seen (sticky)
   -- LED2: SDRAM ACK completed (sticky)
   -- LED3: currently pending (live)
-  LED(0) <= not dbg_leds(0);
-  LED(1) <= not dbg_leds(1);
-  LED(2) <= not dbg_leds(2);
-  LED(3) <= not dbg_leds(3);
+  LED(0) <= dbg_leds(0);
+  LED(1) <= dbg_leds(1);
+  LED(2) <= dbg_leds(2);
+  LED(3) <= dbg_leds(3);
 
   -- ── Wishbone → SDRAM bridge ───────────────────────────────────────────────
   -- ── XBUS mux (SHA / ASMI / REMOTE / SDRAM) ────────────────────────────
